				<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>As their brand turns 30, the design duo <strong>Dolce &#038; Gabbana</strong>, have something to say. And interviewed by <a href="http://www.harpersbazaar.com/culture/features/dolce-and-gabbana-interview-0215" target="_blank">Harper&#8217;s Bazaar</a>, they also talked the first time they met <strong>Madonna</strong>.<br />
Check it out:</p>
<p><em>Christine Whitney: What stars do you most admire?</p>
<p>Domenico Dolce: I love Italian actresses—women with strong personalities like Anna Magnani and Sophia Loren.</p>
<p>Stefano Gabbana: We&#8217;ve worked with Isabella Rossellini, Monica Bellucci, and <strong>Madonna</strong>. In the beginning, we were in Torino to watch Madonna&#8217;s concert, and <strong>we dreamed that one day she would wear our clothes</strong>. <strong>Later I found a picture of her in Dolce &#038; Gabbana—I touched the sky with my finger. </strong>Our first meeting was in New York in an Italian restaurant on 17th Street. I was very nervous—we were waiting to meet our icon! At the time you could still smoke in restaurants, and I was sweating and took out one cigarette after another. <strong>She was filming Dick Tracy, and arrived in a man&#8217;s suit with a little hat. I fell in love.</strong></em></p>
<p>The post <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com/dolce-gabbana-saw-madonna-wearing-clothes-touched-sky-finger/20150109">Dolce &#038; Gabbana: &#8220;When we saw Madonna wearing our clothes we touched the sky with our finger!&#8221;</a> appeared first on <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com">Madonna news new album Rebel Heart</a>.</p>
